> **Template v4.5.2** (2026-09-01): initialization reliability and diagnostics. Three Core scripts lost mechanical defects: `prepare-apm-packages.ps1` no longer aborts under Windows PowerShell 5.1 when git writes progress to stderr (and now prints which registry source it resolved), `validate-doc-links.js` no longer crashes on a deleted tracked file and gained `--scope`, and `compute-hashes.ps1/.sh` accept `"optional": true` in `coreFiles`. Two new gates catch states that reported success while producing nothing: `validate-apm-install.ps1` (a poisoned `apm.lock.yaml` entry makes every later `apm install` print `(files unchanged)` and deploy nothing) and `check-guidelines-specificity.js` (a rendered `guidelines.md` full of generalities passes the placeholder check and is useless at runtime). `/docs-sync` gained a mandatory Project-Mode context skill sync — `project-config.json` first, then re-render `guidelines.md` from it. Every bare `pwsh` invocation became `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File …`. The offline registry snapshot was regenerated (19 → 21 packages). Migration `v4.5.2-init-reliability`. See [CHANGELOG.md](mdc:../../CHANGELOG.md).
